{
  "requirement": "The SDK MUST supply a filesystem-backed evidence-storage helper to which an\n`EvidenceStorage` implementation can delegate its `load_evidence` and\n`store_evidence` methods under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation: the SDK MUST supply a filesystem-backed helper that an `EvidenceStorage` implementation can delegate `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` to.\n\n- **Delegation.** `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs` is marked `{test}` for the subject. It builds `StoredGraph`, a real `EvidenceStorage` impl whose `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` forward to `FileEvidenceStorage::load` and `FileEvidenceStorage::store`. The test calls them through the trait.\n- **Behavior asserted through the delegated methods.**\n  - Loading a missing node returns `Ok(None)`.\n  - After a store, the load returns the same dependencies and output.\n  - A different node still loads as `None`.\n  - Corrupt JSON on disk loads as `Err(FileStorageError::Json(_))`.\n\n  The last two assertions show the helper keeps nodes apart and tells a missing record from an error. That matches the `evidence_storage` rules the subject cites.\n- **Supporting tests.** Other tests in the same file cover the helper itself:\n  - `records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error` checks that the procedure version is preserved and that I/O and JSON errors are reported.\n  - `paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects` checks path mapping and that a missing load has no side effects.\n  - `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` checks Send futures, root creation, and that over-long keys fail with an I/O error rather than being truncated.\n\n  These carry `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.*` markers rather than the subject marker. The subject only requires that the helper exists and is delegable, so I treat them as supporting evidence and not as a marking gap.\n\nI found no obligation in the subject text that the tests leave unchecked.",
  "references": "a7acd7515cb0da8eb4bcf8d281a19c2b8af40b6a81e09f15ac3b27df2c4034e1",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage.filesystem",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage.filesystem"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} evidence_storage.filesystem",
        "The SDK MUST supply a filesystem-backed evidence-storage helper to which an",
        "`EvidenceStorage` implementation can delegate its `load_evidence` and",
        "`store_evidence` methods under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} evidence_storage",
        "`habeas_sdk::graph` MUST expose the following storage interface:",
        "",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "use std::future::Future;",
        "",
        "pub trait EvidenceStorage: Graph {",
        "    fn load_evidence<'a>(",
        "        &'a self,",
        "        node: &'a Self::NodeId,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<",
        "        Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::JudgmentMetadata>>,",
        "        Self::Error,",
        "    >> + Send + 'a;",
        "",
        "    fn store_evidence<'a>(",
        "        &'a self,",
        "        node: &'a Self::NodeId,",
        "        record: &'a Record<Self::NodeId, Self::JudgmentMetadata>,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send + 'a;",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "The node runner MUST use the requested `NodeId` directly for evidence lookup",
        "and persistence. It MUST NOT require a separate evidence-key type or a",
        "procedure name as part of the storage key.",
        "`load_evidence` MUST distinguish an absent record (`Ok(None)`) from a storage",
        "error (`Err`). Storage MUST preserve the record's procedure version,",
        "dependencies, and judgment. The application MUST be able to choose the",
        "persistence mechanism without filesystem paths or a global evidence listing",
        "being required by this interface.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
